                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000-01-01">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000-12-31"/>
                    <occupation>Lawyer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Hugh O'Hanlon, who becomes Law Advisor to the Irish
                            Office in London in 1831. Has a brother, Padraig, Captain in the Bengal
                            Lancers. Both sons of Patrick O'Hanlon, of Newry. Hugh had been active in
                            promoting reform legislation in Ireland in the 1820s. The relationship with Godwin is never intimate. He
                            meets Hugh though Hume, and a lot of the contacts are 'advs' at the
                            theatre. In 1825, (on the third meeting) he names Hugh O'Hanlon - so it is possible that the other
                            mentions - or some other mentions, are to his father or brother. His
                            brother, as Captain O'Hanlon, features in the fashion columns of the newspapers - and
                            might be more probably as the theatre link.</p>
                    </note>
